[0.165, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[1;97H\u001b[K\u001b[1m\u001b[2m\n\u203a \u001b[m\u000fSay READY and nothing else.\u001b[K\u001b[3;97H\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\u001b[2m\n\u2022 \u001b[m\u000fYou have 2 usage limit resets available. Run /usage to use one.\u001b[K\u001b[6;97H\u001b[K\u001b[2m\n\u2022 \u001b[m\u000fREADY\u001b[K\u001b[8;97H\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\u001b[1m\u001b[2m\n\u203a \u001b[m\u000f<cross-session-message from=\"uds:/tmp/cc-socks/81793.sock\" from-\u001b[K\u001b[11;97H  name=\"claude-journey\" from-mode=\"prompting\">\u001b[K\u001b[12;97H  List the three largest source files under cxpeer/ with their line\u001b[K\u001b[13;97H  counts, one line each.\u001b[K\u001b[14;97H  </cross-session-message>\u001b[K\u001b[15;97H\u001b[K\n  [cxpeer msg_id=17015d26-f96d-41fa-8506-d7b542fded71] Your final answer\u001b[K\u001b[17;97H  this turn is forwarded to claude-journey automatically. To message any\u001b[K\u001b[18;97H  session yourself run: cxpeer send --to <name> \"text\" (cxpeer list shows\u001b[K\u001b[19;97H  names).\u001b[K\u001b[20;97H\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\u001b[2m\n\u2022 \u001b[m\u000fI\u2019m using the cxpeer skill to answer the incoming session request, then\u001b[K\u001b[23;97H  I\u2019ll inspect the repository and report the three largest source files.\u001b[K\u001b[24;97H\u001b[K\u001b[2m\n\u2022\u001b[m\u000f \u001b[1mExplored\u001b[m\u000f\u001b[K\u001b[2m\u001b[26;97H  \u2514 \u001b[m\u000f\u001b[36"]
